## Initial Data Import

Import from existing `wine_store` spreadsheet:

| Sheet | Records | Imported As |
|---|---|---|
| **開店前置作業** | 32 tasks | Workflow template + active instance |
| **營業小物件** | 33 items | Operational procurement checklist |

**Seed users:** Zoey, 學文, Ken, 營運

The system will be **pre-populated** with real operational data on Day 1.

---

## Tech Stack

| Component | Technology |
|---|---|
| Database & Auth | Supabase (PostgreSQL) |
| Backend API | Supabase Edge Functions (Deno) |
| AI Assistant | Qwen 3.5 (DashScope API) |
| LINE Integration | LINE Messaging API |
| Admin UI | Vite + React + TypeScript |
| Scheduling | pg_cron |

---

## Key Deliverables

| Phase | Deliverable | Estimated Effort |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Bot responds to LINE messages with AI · Admin login works | Foundation |
| 2 | Create/manage workflows and tasks from admin UI | Core Engine |
| 3 | Full task management from LINE chat in 中文/English | LINE Interface |
| 4 | Auto reminders for overdue tasks · Escalation rules | Notifications |
| 5 | Event → Condition → Action automation from admin UI | Automation |
| 6 | LINE users mapped to system · Group routing active | Identity Layer |

---

## Success Metrics

| Metric | Target |
|---|---|
| Task visibility | 100% of store-opening tasks tracked in one system |
| Response time | LINE commands respond in < 3 seconds |
| Reminder coverage | Every overdue task triggers a notification |
| User adoption | Team manages daily tasks via LINE, not spreadsheets |
| AI utility | Natural language queries return actionable data |

---

## Future Expansion (Post-MVP)

The foundation supports scaling into:

| Module | Description |
|---|---|
| Inventory Management | Stock tracking, purchase orders, vendor management |
| Employee & HR | Attendance, scheduling, leave requests |
| Marketing | Campaign management, promotion tracking |
| Finance | Sales reporting, expense tracking, P&L |
| Analytics & Dashboards | Real-time KPIs per store, executive reports |
| Multi-store RBAC | Role-based access per store, department, region |

> The MVP builds the **operational backbone** — every future module plugs into the same workflow, task, and notification infrastructure.
